=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.12$ | $0.23$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X+Y=1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y=1) & =P(X=0,Y=1)+P(X=1,Y=0) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,0) \\\\  & =0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109687/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109686"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X=0,Y=1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110934/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "3ed8b1c1-4f93-5a3c-95d4-5988893ec1f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110934/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "1971df0e-9669-5786-8162-bb43ba07275c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110934/selection/dc3495771514bafee34c33b48bc7b9d0a2d595f84c8c5c6c2219eb4b14e557be" :answer/id #uuid "ebfc6446-a4f9-5e4c-a63f-d9bee626e9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{64}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110934/sele