6be118-3237-5a6d-bb73-42ee9dce8ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-111080" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<3\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,3)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(3,3)) \\\\  & =f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.15+0.3+0.15 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" :answer/id #uuid "bed37fe7-ac0d-581e-927c-e1eb23b6085e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "1db6068d-4a9b-50ed-844c-e3e4dae7b8f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "168b07ef-264c-51e9-9152-c48239a92234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "f611bd8d-e965-5740-bd78-5912a1f6ce70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection/250d79f96fe0538363a39ff6475c3291963c6a55bc727ce128daeb62e061a964" :answer/id #uuid "c5ba6b5c-ff60-5b34-a0af-9bdacdd0f4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f87787d-dc49-51d0-8813-8cf6df012033" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111081/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-111081/selection/bd0c5293c05dbcd56341c67931e9e0ae46e20e1d0de3da140e1b2dcd87ea42e2" "q-111081/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-111081/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-111081/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-111081/selection/250d79f96fe0538363a39ff6475c3291963c6a55bc727ce128daeb62e061a964"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111081" :question/id #uuid "87831530-3a25-531e-9050-ede8e0edb856" :question/math-academy-id "q-111081" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,0)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.15+0.1+0.05+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111081/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111081"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109337"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,2),(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6))+P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-109336"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "a68bf074-8843-576f-8be3-003edb5c91c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "aab664d5-16f8-53d0-bbf1-fe261209e5fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer/id #uuid "16d8c98c-55e5-5ee6-8930-388393c14cc9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0" :answer/id #uuid "f7c3699a-7723-50af-825e-cca81fe31162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "34dfa4bb-f428-5716-ac21-8d8d5250a24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4ca3894-8e96-53c6-8a07-6cdc833484d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111076/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-111076/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-111076/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-111076/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" "q-111076/selection/5b6a7457ecf38e757655a8ab80cd7dca24376644ed8b5d929a23fb6af65f88f0" "q-111076/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111076" :question/id #uuid "58ffa5cf-73c4-5d38-bbb0-2b8060cfb4fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-111076" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111076/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111076"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9126"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is $S_X = \\{0,1\\},$ the support of $Y$ is $S_Y = \\{0,1\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0),  (0,1),  (1,0),  (1,1) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(1,0)+f(1,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+a+a+\\frac{5}{2}a & =1 \\\\ 5a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9203"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\Big( (X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(2,3),(6,1)}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9204"] :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\left( X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
